<spell-notebook "segment theming">
	<header level="1">
		Segment
		<header>A segment is used to create a grouping of related content.</>
	</>
	<segment-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-segment-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a `<ui-segments>` group,
			`:root`), or on the box through `::part(segment)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each
			through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. Set on a `<ui-segments>`, they reach its segments.

			- Variations build on them: `padding="md"` swaps in `--ui-segment-padded`, `padding="lg"` `--ui-segment-very-padded`.
			- `--ui-segment-scrolling-height` replaces the viewport-based height of `scrolling` segments at every width.
			- The group's own `--_ui-segments-*` tokens, and every `--_segment-*` / `--_ui-segment-*` name, are private
			  plumbing: never set them.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* square segments in one group */
			ui-segments.cards {
			  --ui-segment-radius: 0;
			}
			/* taller scrolling segments everywhere */
			:root {
			  --ui-segment-scrolling-height: 20em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-segment" playground>
				<ui-segment>
					<p>Te eum doming eirmod, nominati pertinacia argumentum ad his.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
